info.additionalInfo:
Make sure to set ChatGPT to dark mode. For the best result add the following to the systemprompt:
"Use headings (#, ##, ###, etc.) to structure responses logically and break down information into sections.
Bold key points, terms, or important ideas.
Use italic to emphasize words or phrases.
Keep responses clear, structured, and easy to read with compact formatting."
It gives you more contrast, by giving the different formatting different colours. If you want to customize the theme, you need to delete it first and then before installing go to the customisation options and chose the custom variant. Then you can set colours for the for the different headings and formatings. If you are familiar with css you can also edit the installed style and  add the following snipped to the top of the code. There will be errors beacuse of the linthing settings of sylish, but it works anyways.
:root {
--background-color: 'add color here';
  --strong-color: 'add color here';
  --em-color: 'add color here';
  --h1-color: 'add color here';
  --h2-color: 'add color here';
  --h3-color: 'add color here';
  --h4-color: 'add color here';
  --h5-color: 'add color here';
  --h6-color: 'add color here';
}

style.css:
@-moz-document domain("chatgpt.com"), domain("chat.openai.com") {
:root {
  --background-color: #2e3440;
  --strong-color: #ebcb8b;
  --em-color: #88c0d0;
  --h1-color: #bf616a;
  --h2-color: #a3be8c;
  --h3-color: #b48ead;
  --h4-color: #b48ead;
  --h5-color: #8fbcbb;
  --h6-color: #ebcb8b;
}

body {
  background-color: var(--background-color, /*[[background-color]]*/) !important;
}

/* General styles for strong and em */
strong {
  color: var(--strong-color, /*[[strong-color]]*/) !important;
}

em {
  color: var(--em-color, /*[[em-color]]*/) !important;
}

/* Specific styles for headings */
h1 strong, h1 em,
h2 strong, h2 em,
h3 strong, h3 em,
h4 strong, h4 em,
h5 strong, h5 em,
h6 strong, h6 em {
  color: inherit !important; /* or set to a specific color for headings */
}

/* Specific colors for headings */
h1 {
  color: var(--h1-color, /*[[h1-color]]*/) !important;
}

h2 {
  color: var(--h2-color, /*[[h2-color]]*/) !important;
}

h3 {
  color: var(--h3-color, /*[[h3-color]]*/) !important;
}

h4 {
  color: var(--h4-color, /*[[h4-color]]*/) !important;
}

h5 {
  color: var(--h5-color, /*[[h5-color]]*/) !important;
}

h6 {
  color: var(--h6-color, /*[[h6-color]]*/) !important;
}
}
